     1,
     "I would like to plot a density function with fill between the curve and the 0 axis over some interval on the X axis.  Is there a good way to do this?<p>So far I have been manually creating a dataset with points along the curve and initial and final points with Y=0, and then using geom_polygon.<p>stat_function gives me the curve, but not the fill AFAIK.<p>I&#39;m using an old version of ggplot2, 0.8.9.<p>Thanks.<br>Ross Boylan</p></p></p></p>"
    ]
